{
 "flight": "STS-134, Endeavour",
 "notes": [
  "STS-134's flown entry-guidance I-loads in G3's #PCGGC03, from DASS_G3.ASC's PATCH SUMMARY (the flown G3 load against the generic tape): every word whose value in a G3 memory image (abort11-tal-bank's OPS 3 capture, volume eeaf4636) is the generic (LM) one and whose flown (MM) value differs -- 269 halfwords, the whole csect's flown set but two (CGGS_VYLMAX, CGGS_Y1: neither LM nor MM in memory, left alone).",
  "Among them: CGGS_ASTART 5.66 -> 4.25 ft/s^2 (the drag that ends pre-entry, GGEENT), VA1, VB1, DF, D230, RPTI, AK, AK1, ZK1, CY0, the alpha table (CALP0/1/2, VALP), the TAL alpha ramp (VALPD1 1600 -> 2000, VALPD2 800 -> 1750, VNOALP2 25000 -> 21000), VNOALP, and the TAEM terms (ENBIAS, X_HAC_LOW/HIGH_MASS, H_DECAY, SB_REF, TAU_GAMMA, QBG2, N_FADER, ...).",
  "Why: a TAL entry on the generic values held the wings level through the pull-out (a skip to 227 kft) and rolled in to 120 deg at q 40 psf; the yaw jets could not hold the sideslip and ran the aft pods dry (abort9/abort11, 2026-10-10).  G3 is also the NOMINAL entry's: re-fly both.",
  "Placement: flat = address + 1,139,262, the G3 load block that also holds #PCGNFL1 (CGNS_TAL_PRIME_AREA's G3 copy); 715 of the csect's 831 words in the image match the volume there.  Applied on -full2 to make -full3."
 ],
